  "Slice Route A with 1 wall loop, no top/bottom, no infill; the preview must show one continuous line per wall.",
  "Full 360° domes are printable again: the closed-revolve seam (chord ring putting both crossovers on one angle, plus a web pattern that did not tile the turn) was fixed 2026-08-26 and is locked by tests T16a-f. Verified 0 overlaps at 180/270/360° for every web grammar, with jitter, with grading and with width modulation up to amp 2.",
  "Dome density still has a floor the node-gap check does not catch: on the R60 dome λ=5 and λ=6 collide (27 and 1 overlaps at 360°, 99 and 72 at 270°) while passing the gap floor. λ>=7 is clean. The independent overlap detector, not the floor, is what makes this safe — curvature is not in the floor's formula.",
  "On a closed revolve λ is QUANTISED: the pitch is snapped so a whole number of waves fits the turn (rounded to a multiple of 16 half-waves so dyadic LOD keeps dividing it). At R60, λ=9 and λ=10 both land on the same effective 9.42 mm. The snap is bounded to 10% of the requested λ by test T1b.",
  "Lean grading measured identical to dyadic auto-LOD on this dome at λ=8 and λ=16 (same weld count, same thread length to the millimetre). It is a stated policy, not a different outcome, in this window."
